       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the usual maximum.\n\n- **Single dose:** 1600 mg is double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg.\n- **Daily total:** 6,400 mg/day is well above the 3,200 mg/day maximum for adults under supervision. The OTC limit is 1,200 mg/day.\n- **Risk:** A dose this high raises the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. Normal kidney and liver function and no allergies don't change that.\n\nHere are some common regimens that may be what you meant:\n- 400 mg by mouth every 6 hours (1,600 mg/day total)\n- 600 mg by mouth every 6 hours (2,400 mg/day total)\n- 800 mg by mouth three times daily (2,400 mg/day total)\n- 800 mg by mouth four times daily (3,200 mg/day total, the maximum, usually for inflammatory conditions)\n\nDid you mean 1,600 mg per day in total, or one of the regimens above? If you do want the original dose, tell me the clinical rationale and I'll proceed as you direct. Tell me the dose and frequency and I'll enter it."
      }
